    },
    "body": "The compensation candidate now reaches its correct first token on two more development rows, yet retains only eight complete replies. This change captures the actual next-step computation on failed row 399 and successful controls 5 and 13, all at the same reached prefix `[617]`, so the next learning decision can use the actual bank, bridge, Generate factors and pooled Copy/Generate output.\n\nThe example reloads the authenticated compensation artifact and runs exactly three production native steps. It emits complete physical occurrence/provenance, bank and sidecar traces, categorical bridge scores and transport, all 4,096 Generate factor decompositions per frame and the full integer output pools. Targets are attached after all captures; saved canonical parity metadata is never supplied to model inputs or selection. No runtime model source, artifact parameters, training rule or selector changes.\n\nRow 399's target 2097 loses to 3817 by 35 Generate-code units (2.1875 nats), with unary/pair/bias contributions −37/−12/+14. Both tokens have only Generate mass. All three have identical query/prefix U state but different factual states. Donor relations are 1, 1 and 2 respectively; the successful relation-1 control prevents diagnosing a bad donor from the failure alone. Expected source-role correctness remains unresolved.\n\nValidation at executed source `0c5c7257233527a51bb8254ba3f4695d27c0fbfe`: formatting, five focused example tests and release build pass. Mathematical and adversarial source reviews pass. An independent saved reader reconstructs all 12,288 Generate scores, categorical bridge actions/transport, physical Copy sums, provenance and full alias-pooled masses. Actual Rust complete-file verification passes for capture, compensation parent and input panel. The reader does not independently rerun Context/cue/prefix learned kernels or tokenization. Exact final-head checks and review are posted separately before queue admission.\n\nRuntime: private `caseyallard/uor-r4-store`, revision `03cec37ef15e22210433b6ed36cb0cb46866f47f`, prefix `codex/sol-reached-prefix/runtime-0c5c725723-attempt2`.\n\nAudited result: revision `51abff40d6fb1ee9d2e6a6edd9e8b4cb849d167b`, prefix `codex/sol-reached-prefix/reached-prefix-0001-0c5c725723`. Archive SHA256 `758185d89fa6722948b9ddf3a91f2f73998bae7005e18976be5ab84d1ecd98f3`, 1,158,382 bytes. Every published file was freshly downloaded and hash verified. Report `be6d6c8f807bd7c3a5c477e060828221611fbe882967390e2bba99b34fdcbf1e`, seal `b94a78279acf01973ea85588945a696916ff590c1c63ac62cb82da35b05216dd`.\n\nProducer pre-seal time 21.219540s; supervisor 30.137359s; peak RSS 184,300 KiB. Independent reader 26.404939s; three Rust seal checks 19.012293s. Cumulative projection increases 443670→454470 seconds, retaining preparation, setup defects, prior charges and unavailable legacy timing. Work used two pod CPU threads; no laptop model/build or large artifact download.\n\nA saved prototype bound clears a necessary condition for a future once-adjacent shared-action U discriminator (eight differing lanes, maximum raw improvement 64 versus gap 35). This derived check was made after archive publication and is retained separately in repository evidence/final delivery. Full-pool preservation feasibility is unresolved and learning is not admitted by this PR. No new complete-reply, useful chat, transfer, energy or capacity result is claimed.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
